# Weekly secret audit of $HOME critical paths (dotfiles, ~/bin, ~/repos,
# AI session logs). It scans and pages; it never masks (sd:1254).
#
# scan-for-secrets exits 2 on durable findings, which counts as a job
# failure here on purpose: it triggers the failure notification (macOS
# banner + ntfy push), so a leak reaches your phone. Agent scratchpads and
# ~/.codex/shell_snapshots read as transient: printed, never paged on.
#
# Masking is a manual operator step, not part of this job. mask rewrites a
# file in place on the same inode, and a session that resumes while it runs
# can append between mask's last check and its truncate; the line is lost.
# Run by hand, that is a risk the operator can time; unattended, it is not
# (operator ruling 2026-10-07). To clear the accepted values from the
# session logs, run a dry run, read it, then apply:
#   scan-for-secrets.sh mask --no-prune
#   scan-for-secrets.sh mask --apply --no-prune
# Sessions keep echoing exported keys into new log lines, so the page comes
# back after a mask until those keys leave the shell environment
# (local-scan-for-secrets/README.md, "Accepted exposure").
# Output in logs/secret-scan-weekly.log.
JOB_SCHEDULE="0 7 * * 1"
JOB_COMMAND="sh \"$ROOT/../local-scan-for-secrets/scan-for-secrets.sh\" critical"
